<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Babylonian invasion of Egypt (601 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">601 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as failed invasion of Egypt in 601</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Babylonian invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 601 BCE was an attempt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a> to invade Egypt. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-chronicles">Babylonian Chronicles</a>, the battle with the Egyptian army resulted in heavy losses on both sides, and Nebuchadnezzar withdrew. The setback encouraged unrest among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>.</p></div>
